// prelude unit limits (DESIGN.md step M0.11, written by that step): the
// minimum depth of nested calls the evaluator reaches. A conforming compiler
// never rejects an evaluation for nesting calls this deep. There is no minimum
// of steps or of memory, since no count of either may stop compile-time
// evaluation: checking code runs only when it is total by algebraic evidence,
// and the program's static calls run under the partial-evaluation budgets
// (author, 2026-11-09). The Rust-hosted copy is
// zed_kernel::eval::MIN_NESTED_CALLS in crates/zed-kernel/src/eval.rs.

// Calls nested in one another.
minNestedCalls = 20000;
